  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 300 PM MST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nSunday...Dry with zonal flow aloft and minimal low and mid level \nmoisture. A bit colder than Saturday with maxima in the upper 30s to \nlower 40s and 700 mb temperatures near -5 Celsius.\n\nMonday...Next neutrally tilted shortwave trough approaches from \nwestern Wyoming with the flow aloft turning southwest, and \nincreasing chances for orographic snows across our Snowy and Sierra \nMadre Ranges. Progressive nature of the shortwave trough aloft \nsuggests snowfall amounts below Winter Weather Advisory criteria.\n\nTuesday...As the trough aloft moves eastward to the Great Plains \nstates, our flow aloft turns northerly, with dry conditions in the \nwake of the perturbation. Continued near normal temperatures with \nhighs in the mid 30s to mid 40s and 700 mb temperatures near -6 \nCelsius.\n\nWednesday...The progressive pattern, synoptically, continues with a \nhigh amplitude ridge aloft moving overhead and keeping our weather \nhigh and dry. Warmer temperatures return with ridging aloft for \nWednesday through Friday.\n\nThanksgiving...The next shortwave trough aloft sweeps to an Idaho to \nFour Corners line, with southerly flow aloft over our neck of the \nwoods. Low and mid level moisture looks sufficient for scattered \norographic snows for our Snowy and Sierra Madre Ranges, and dry \nelsewhere. Decent day for the holiday with maxima in the 40s to \nlower 50s.\n\nFriday...Split shortwave trough energy with the northern piece \ntraveling across the Dakotas by suppertime, and a closed low over \nNew Mexico. Thus, we will be in the dry sector in between.",
